    "result_text": "The build is green. The test suite passes (1 test run, 0 failures/errors, BUILD SUCCESS).\n\nHere's what I implemented to reject creating an owner whose lower-cased email duplicates an existing owner's, responding with 409:\n\n1. **`OwnerRepository`** \u2014 added `existsByEmailIgnoreCase(String email)`. Under the active `spring-data-jpa` profile this is derived automatically by Spring Data.\n\n2. **`JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl`** & **`JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl`** \u2014 added concrete implementations (`LOWER(email) = LOWER(:email)`) so all repository profiles still compile and behave consistently.\n\n3. **`ClinicService` / `ClinicServiceImpl`** \u2014 added `existsOwnerWithEmail(String email)`, guarding against null/blank email (owners without an email are unaffected, matching the many existing tests that create owners with no email).\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added a check mirroring the existing telephone-conflict check: if an owner with the same email already exists, return `409 CONFLICT`.\n\nThe email comparison is case-insensitive both at the query level (`LOWER(...)`) and because `Owner.setEmail` already lower-cases stored values, matching the spec's \"lower-cased email\" wording.",
