    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a clean, additive mirror of the existing `existsOwnerWithTelephone` / `existsByTelephone` feature across every layer:\n\n- **Repository** (`OwnerRepository` + both `Jdbc`/`Jpa` impls): new `existsByEmailIgnoreCase` sits right next to `existsByTelephone`, with the same signature, Javadoc style, and query idiom (`LOWER(...) = LOWER(...)`) matching the established count-based existence pattern.\n- **Service** (`ClinicService` + impl): `existsOwnerWithEmail` follows the same `@Transactional(readOnly = true)` wrapper convention and delegates to the repository \u2014 the right place for this logic.\n- **Controller**: the 409 check is placed alongside the sibling telephone conflict check in `addOwner`, exactly where a maintainer would expect it.\n\nNothing is duplicated, no class is turning into a catch-all, and each piece of logic lives in its correct unit. The extra null/blank guard in the service impl is a minor, harmless deviation from the telephone method (which has none) and reads as a reasonable defensive touch rather than misplaced logic. A maintainer of this codebase would find the structure natural.",
